#: desc: The parser state after each line of Makefile.recipeprefix-conditional (the prefix stays a tab)
#: trace
test/fixtures/Makefile.recipeprefix-conditional
#: stdout
== test/fixtures/Makefile.recipeprefix-conditional
   1 0 0  0  0 \t | # .RECIPEPREFIX is always defined (empty, with origin default): ?= does not change it, so
   2 0 0  0  0 \t | # the recipe lines below start with a tab
   3 0 0  0  0 \t | .RECIPEPREFIX ?= >
   4 0 0  0  0 \t |
   5 0 0  1  0 \t | ## Doc of a
   6 0 1  0  0 \t | a:
   6 ============ => target:[a]
   7 0 1  0  0 \t | \t@echo a
   8 0 1  0  0 \t | \t## a comment for the shell, not a doc
   9 0 1  0  0 \t |
  10 0 1  1  0 \t | ## Doc of b
  11 0 1  0  0 \t | b:
  11 ============ => target:[b]
  12 0 1  0  0 \t | \t@echo b
